Based on my analysis of the panoramic radiograph, I identified the residual dentition (a root-canal-treated tooth with a crown in the maxillary region and a 3-unit mandibular bridge) and localized the periapical bone changes at their apices.

{"lesions": [{"box": [0.409, 0.364, 0.469, 0.495], "pai": 4}, {"box": [0.448, 0.627, 0.532, 0.743], "pai": 4}]}

Notes on confidence: the radiograph is low-contrast and heavily blurred, so lesion margins are ill-defined. Both sites show localized radiolucency in bone contiguous with the root apices (consistent with PAI 4 — well-defined radiolucent areas). The remaining edentulous regions show no focal periapical lucencies.
